That’s where Expo Image Picker fits. It’s the official Expo library for opening the system UI to choose images and videos from the device library or take a photo with the camera, as described in the Expo package repository. In practice, that means you get a reliable bridge into native media input, but not a custom media experience that behaves identically on every device.
This guide is written for the first implementation, not the demo. It focuses on the decisions that matter in production: managed versus bare workflow setup, permission handling that won’t surprise you later, safe result parsing, and a practical upload pattern after the user picks a file. If you’re working in a custom native setup, it also helps to understand how this differs from an Expo development client workflow.

